WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.022
The Dazhongsi AI Industry Cluster covers a provisional rough boundary of about 0.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:28.044
720 million square meters, derived from the announcement text extents.

00:00:28.044 --> 00:00:42.067
The proposal uses a time-shifted envelope in which industry hosting and community service share the same physical infrastructure: daytime hours are oriented toward research and incubation work, while evenings and weekends convert the same spaces into community sports, cultural, and public service programming for nearby residents.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:01:02.100
AI compute centers, research workstations, and incubation offices share the same physical boundary as the vegetable market, the childcare center, and the senior canteen — the two communities are deliberately not separated into different districts but are scheduled through the same municipal interface. When off-peak dispatch fails for any reason, the schedule falls back to manual time windows rather than disabling any basic public service window, so the most essential community services remain uninterrupted regardless of the AI system's status.

